# Personal Itineraries Platform

Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/README.md` before large changes.

## Hard rules

- Domain: personal itineraries + Colombian airports. Not Parche.
- Stack: Next.js frontend (shadcn/ui + Sonner, feature folders), Go backends, RabbitMQ, Redis, Postgres per service.
- Frontend: put primitives in `components/ui`, screens in `features/*/`, shared HTTP in `lib/api`. Never call API Colombia from the browser.
- Hexagonal per Go service; Adapter for API Colombia; Gateway has no business logic.
- Transactional Outbox for integration events (no unsafe dual write).
- HARD RULE: every change → branch from `main` → Pull Request → merge into `main`. Never commit/push directly to `main` (includes docs and agent edits). See `AGENTS.md`.
- Update `docs/` in the same PR when architecture or behavior changes. Wiki pages (`wiki/`) are Spanish prose; keep filenames and code identifiers in English.
- Conventional Commits in English.

## Phase awareness

If application code is still absent, prefer docs/ADR PRs over inventing undeclared services.
